{
  "company_name": "AssemblyGuard Systems",
  "industry": "Computer & Electronic",
  "use_case": "Predictive maintenance and troubleshooting for electronics assembly lines",
  "space_title": "AssemblyGuard Systems - Predictive Maintenance 🔧",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Computer & Electronic\n\n**Use case:** Predictive Maintenance & Troubleshooting\n\nAssemblyGuard Systems — sensor-driven reliability analytics across SMT and electronics assembly lines for the EMS Plant Manager, Maintenance Director, and CFO. Operations uses this space to triage live anomalies, compare predicted vs corrective work orders, and find chronic bad-actor machines; finance uses it to size unplanned-downtime exposure and justify PdM program ROI against the typical 12-18 month payback.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- MTBF (hours) — reliability KPI; PdM typically lifts MTBF 20-40%\n- MTTR (hours) — repair speed; planned PdM repairs run 40-60% faster than emergency\n- Availability (%) — uptime; world-class OEE availability 90%+\n- Total downtime hours — direct capacity loss; 60% of SMT downtime is feeder/nozzle\n- Maintenance cost ($) — PdM programs cut total maintenance cost 10-25%\n- Prediction accuracy (%) — model quality; drives PdM coverage expansion\n- Critical alert count — leading indicator for unplanned events\n- Average anomaly score — fleet health pulse\n\n**Data sources**\n- `sensor_readings` — high-frequency vibration / temperature / power / anomaly readings per machine\n- `maintenance_records` — work-order history with failure mode, downtime, cost, and whether the event was predicted\n- `equipment_health_monthly` — monthly MTBF / MTTR / availability / cost / prediction accuracy rollup",
  "schema_basename": "ce_predictive_maint",
