  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Predictive Maintenance for an electronics assembly operator running multiple SMT and final-assembly lines instrumented with vibration, temperature, and power sensors. Stakeholders include the Plant Manager (availability, downtime, alert triage), Maintenance Director (MTBF, MTTR, PdM coverage) and CFO (maintenance cost, unplanned-downtime exposure, PdM ROI).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- MTBF = mtbf_hours on equipment_health_monthly; PdM programs typically lift MTBF 20-40%.\n- MTTR = mttr_hours on equipment_health_monthly; planned PdM repairs ~40-60% faster than emergency.\n- Availability = availability_pct; world-class OEE availability 90%+ in electronics.\n- Downtime = total_downtime_hours; top SMT failure modes include Nozzle Clog, Solder Contamination, Thermal Drift, and Motor Burnout.\n- Anomaly score = anomaly_score on sensor_readings; high score with critical alert_level drives intervention.\n- Maintenance cost = maintenance_cost_usd; PdM cuts total maintenance cost 10-25%.\n- Prediction accuracy = prediction_accuracy_pct on equipment_health_monthly; was_predicted on maintenance_records flags whether a corrective event was forecast.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - sensor_readings_metrics (source: sensor_readings) — dims: reading_date, machine_type, assembly_line, alert_level; measures: total_readings, avg_vibration, avg_temperature, critical_alert_count, total_power_consumption_kw, total_anomaly_score, unique_machine_count, max_vibration_mm_s.\n  - equipment_health_metrics (source: equipment_health_monthly) — dims: health_month, machine_type, assembly_line; measures: avg_mtbf_hours, avg_mttr_hours, avg_availability_pct, total_maintenance_cost, total_total_downtime_hours, total_prediction_accuracy_percent, unique_machine_count, max_mtbf_hours.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. machine_id, failure_mode, was_predicted, repair_cost_usd, parts_replaced).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly MTBF and availability trend by machine type for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which 10 machines have the highest total downtime hours and maintenance cost this year?",
    "What share of corrective maintenance events were correctly predicted, by assembly line?",
    "Top 10 failure modes by repair cost over the last quarter — and how many of them were predicted?",
    "How has prediction accuracy trended month-over-month across the fleet?",
    "Which assembly lines have availability below 90%, and what is the projected maintenance cost to close the gap?",
    "How many critical sensor alerts were raised by machine type over the last 30 days, and which machines are repeat offenders?"
